#: rc.cpp:794
msgid ""
"Heating coils are used to heat flawsks and other containers. Furthermore, a lot "
"heating coils can be connected with a thermometer so that the heat won't exceed "
"a specified temperature. Using an magnetic field inside the plate it is "
"possible to stir fluids with a magnetic stir bar. This will homogenize the "
"fluid in terms of temperature and composition."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:795
msgid ""
"Ring made of corc are used to place bigger containers like round-bottomed "
"flasks."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:796
msgid ""
"Using a dropping funnel it is easy to drop precise amounts of of fluid into "
"something. With a valve you can control the speed"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:797
msgid ""
"Using a separating funnel you can disperse chemical phases of fluids because of "
"their different density. After a while one can use a valve to let the "
"bottom-phase go."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:798
msgid ""
"Such a rack comes handy if you want to test a lot small amounts of chemicals in "
"a row or if you want to dry test tubes."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:799
msgid ""
"A vortexer serves to homogenise matters at laboratories. Thereto the pot with "
"the matters to homogenise is put on a crust. This one begins to shake with up "
"to 3000 turns by a contact sensor. Thereby extreme little fluids can be "
"homogenised well and quick, too."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:800
msgid ""
"These bottles are used for a lot of purposes. In most laboratories you will "
"find water, salt acid or other commonly used fluids in them. They make it easy "
"to access the fluid if the amount you use is not that important."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:801
msgid ""
"A rotary evaporator consists of a round flask into a bath of hot water. The "
"flask is rotating whereby the dissolver forms a thin film. This one evaporates "
"and condenses again in a reflux condenser. The condensate is intercepted in an "
"other pot. That way solutions can be concentrated and/ or cleaned. Through a "
"affliated vacuum pump the fluid's boiling point can be decreased again."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:802
msgid ""
"A reflux condenser serves to anneal a gas phase during an experiment. As a rule "
"it is put on round-bottom or several neck flasks. Gas which arise from heat "
"addition attain to the reflux condenser, whose walls are rinsed thoroughly with "
"cold water. Thereby the gas is refrigerated. Finally it condenses and attains "
"back to the room of reaction."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:803
msgid ""
"A pileusball is used to fill pipettes. It produces a negative pressure which "
"makes the fluid go into the pipette. If one lets air back into the ball the "
"fluid will run out of the pipette."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:804
msgid ""
"In test tube a chemist usually performs small reaktions. There a lots of "
"differnet tubs, for example those with and without grinding."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:805
msgid ""
"Most labarotories insist that everyone is wearing protective gooles. Without "
"them it is to risky to work with most chemicals. Usually, their glass is some "
"kind of specific plastic which protects you from mechanical impats as well as "
"acids and bases."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:806
msgid ""
"A round-bottomed flask is used for a lot of reaktions. They can be connected to "
"other items, most of them are grinded. With corc rings they can be placed on a "
"table."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:807
msgid ""
"Unlike a regular pipette, a full pipette only has one marking for a specific "
"volume."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:808
msgid ""
"There are reactions which need to be keept free of water. To make this possible "
"one uses a drying tube. In it there is a hygroscopic chemical which will absorb "
"all water."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:809
msgid ""
"With a test tube fastener you can easily hold test tubes. If you use a fastener "
"there is a safe distance between the hand and the test tube and the tube can be "
"hot. In particular it is use when you brandisha test tube over an open flame."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:810
msgid ""
"In a graduate you can fill amounts of liquids relatively precise. Furthermore a "
"graduate serves to let sack particulate matter. Following you can separate them "
"from the fluid by decanting."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:811
msgid ""
"With a thermometer you can determine the temperature. In a laboratory special "
"thermometers are used, which can also be used within acids or bases."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:812
msgid ""
"Magnetic stir bars are chemically nearly unassailable little magnetic bars. "
"Most heaters have a built-in magnet which can rotate. Through this rotation the "
"magnetic stir bars are spinned and the solution the magnetic stir bar is in is "
"homogenised."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:813
msgid ""
"To separate a mixture you can use distillation among others. The distillation "
"bridge is thereby the way between the two pots. In the one pot there is the "
"mixture to be separated. Caused by heating a gas forms which is lead through "
"the bridge. At the end of the bridge the gas phase is condensed again and drips "
"in a round flask. As a rule  the bridge is cooled by return flow. In addition "
"there is often a thermometer for controlling the temperature on the "
"distillation bridge."
msgstr ""

